verdicts.corrections:
I fetched the PDF (HTTP 200, 2.7 MB). It confirms:
- 'No. 21 | 16 October 2025' and ISSN 2078-0796;
- 423.9 +/-0.2 ppm, 1942 +/-2 ppb and 338.0 +/-0.1 ppb;
- 152%, 266% and 125% of pre-industrial;
- a 3.5 ppm rise, 'the largest one-year increase since modern measurements began in 1957';
- a methane lifetime of 'about nine years';
- 'achieving net-zero anthropogenic CO2 emissions must be the focus of climate action'.

WDCGG policy page (gaw.kishou.go.jp/policy/gaw): 'WDCGG Data Archive content is free and unrestricted'. The GAW policy says 'For Scientific purposes, access to these data is unlimited and provided without charge', with an expected offer of co-authorship. There is no CC licence, so 'unclear' for public redistribution of the data stands. Citing the bulletin's numbers as facts is fine.

I could not check whether No. 22 exists (search budget exhausted). Historically it comes in Oct/Nov, so re-check late Oct 2026.
